  partName: Bolt (10)
  description: The Bolt (10) is a tiny, complex-shaped fastener located at the top-center-rear
    of the engine, playing a crucial role in securing various components together.
    Its small size belies its importance, as it helps maintain the structural integrity
    of the engine. Interestingly, the Bolt (10) is made of Material.001, a durable
    material capable of withstanding high temperatures and stresses.
